<title>UK: Liberty current sales up around nine pct.</title>
<headline>Liberty current sales up around nine pct.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>British retailer Liberty Plc said on Thursday the year had started satisfactorily and that sales were currently running around nine percent ahead of last year.  </p>
<p>Chairman Denis Cassidy told shareholders at the company's annual meeting, &quot;The strength of pound in the foreign exchange markets has had an adverse effect on revenues from tourists as well as income.&quot;</p>
<p>However, he noted that the rise in domestic sales had more than compensated &quot;for this loss which we hope will prove to be temporary.&quot;</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 4019</p>
</text>
